+{
+  "task_id": "session-migration/transfer",
+  "repository": "earendil-works/pi",
+  "mode": "repair",
+  "validation": {
+    "command": "node --experimental-vm-modules .prale-eval/regression.mjs",
+    "status": "passed",
+    "notes": "Fault located in packages/coding-agent/src/migrations.ts, migrateSessionsFromAgentRoot(): the session directory encoder used cwd.replace(/^[/\\\\]/, \"\").replace(/[/:]/g, \"-\") so backslashes were never replaced; drive-letter cwds such as C:\\Users\\me\\proj became '--C-\\Users\\me\\proj--' and UNC cwds \\\\server\\share\\proj became '--\\server\\share\\proj--', migrating sessions into a wrong directory (session-manager.ts getDefaultSessionDirPath already used the correct /[/\\\\:]/g form). Fix is a one-character-class change to cwd.replace(/^[/\\\\]/, \"\").replace(/[/\\\\:]/g, \"-\") plus nothing else; no other production file was touched (git diff: 1 file, 1 line). .prale-eval/regression.mjs loads the real module through .prale-eval/subject.mjs loadMigrations(root, agentDir) with real fs/path and a temporary agentDir under .prale-eval/.tmp (removed in a finally block), then asserts: POSIX (/home/user/proj -> --home-user-proj--), drive-letter (C:\\Users\\me\\proj -> --C--Users-me-proj--), UNC (\\\\server\\share\\proj -> ---server-share-proj--), colon (/srv/repo:name -> --srv-repo-name--) and CRLF-header (D:\\work\\app -> --D--work-app--) cwds land in the exact expected session directories; session bytes are preserved byte-for-byte including a non-UTF-8 payload (move, not rewrite); invalid headers (non-JSON, missing cwd, non-session type) are ignored and left byte-identical at the agent root; a pre-existing destination file is never overwritten and its source is kept; and two extra runs are idempotent (no duplicate directories, unchanged bytes). Verified the regression is fault-sensitive: with the original /[/:]/g code re-inserted temporarily it fails with AssertionError (exit 1) on the session-directory set, and with the fix it exits 0. Limitation: vitest and typescript are not installed in this workspace (no node_modules) and dependencies were not installed per instructions, so no vitest/tsc run was possible; validation relies on Node 24 built-ins only (stripTypeScriptTypes + vm modules)."
+  }
+}
